    "require_emulator remains before _stop_required assignment and all device-changing commands. Empty ownership slots make entry failure cleanup empty, so shared failure policy rethrows the exact canonical error.",
    "Status-zero missing first property still checks the second; missing both still refuse unless physical-device launch/environment opt-in. Explicit physical opt-in does not waive a failed required emulator query. Cold-boot launch/environment opt-ins still return before the snapshot query; this ordering is byte-exact.",
    "README617-618 and Unreleased Fixed2493-2495 accurately distinguish failed commands from successful missing properties. They add no hardware, native verification or blanket query-policy claim.",
    "Six unchanged required-observation controls protect two raw error identities/no mutation and four healthy/fallback/refusal paths; old opt-in callers are unchanged. Existing mocked RecordingDevice ignores status by design, so source reasoning and the command-boundary controls are complementary."
  ],
